External runtime requirements (not vendored, must be installed separately):
- FFmpeg / ffprobe — required for video audio extraction, subtitle probing, and
  audio export. FFmpeg is licensed under LGPL or GPL depending on build; install
  it from your platform package manager. DeepListener invokes it as an external
  binary and does not redistribute FFmpeg.

Algorithm attribution:
- The spaced-repetition scheduler is the Free Spaced Repetition Scheduler
  (FSRS), used via the MIT-licensed `ts-fsrs` library. DeepListener does not
  redistribute the algorithm source; it calls the library through its public API.

External services (referenced by code, configured by the operator):
- Transcription providers (OpenAI, Deepgram, Google Generative AI) are called
  with API keys the operator provides. DeepListener does not bundle provider
  credentials or redistribute provider content.
- Linear (optional, used by the Symphony orchestrator) is called only if the
  operator provides a LINEAR_API_KEY.
